hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17128","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Laqit, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved, three times: my death, and the Dajjal, and the killing of a caliph patient upon the truth, giving it."
"17129","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Hawalah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting in the shade of a lote tree, and with him was a scribe of his dictating to him. He said: Shall I not write you down, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: I do not know what Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He turned away from me, and Ismail once said in the first: Shall we write you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: I do not know, for what, O Messenger of Allah? He turned away from me and bent over his scribe dictating to him. Then he said: Shall I write you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: I do not know what Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He turned away from me and bent over his scribe dictating to him. He said: I looked, and there in the writing was Umar. I said: Umar is only written in good. Then he said: Shall I write you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: Yes. He said: O Ibn Hawalah, what will you do in a trial emerging in the ends of the earth as if it were the horns of cattle? I said: I do not know what Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He said: And what will you do in another emerging after it, as if the first in it is the puff of a rabbit? I said: I do not know what Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He said: Follow this. He said: And a man turning away at that time. He said: I went and hastened and took hold of his shoulder and turned his face to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: This? He said: Yes. He said: And he was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah Most High be pleased with him."
"17130","Haywah ibn Shurayh and Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Qutaylah, from Ibn Hawalah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The affair will come to be massed troops: a troop in Sham, and a troop in Yemen, and a troop in Iraq. Ibn Hawalah said: Choose for me, O Messenger of Allah, if I reach that. He said: Upon you is Sham, for it is the best of Allah from His land; He gathers to it His best of His servants. If you refuse, then upon you is your Yemen, and drink from your ponds, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has guaranteed me Sham and its people."
"17131","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Laqit, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved, three times: my death, and the Dajjal, and the killing of a caliph patient upon the truth, giving it."
